{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00922",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 0.34,
      "end_seconds": 12.97,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "Doctor, it's our son Rohan, he's three months old. He spits up after every single feed, and I'm worried he isn't keeping enough down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.24,
      "end_seconds": 15.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Waaah. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.67,
      "end_seconds": 30.37,
      "duration_seconds": 13.7,
      "text": "Hello, little man. Thank you both for bringing him. Let me hear it from you first, Mum. How often does he spit up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 31.44,
      "end_seconds": 35.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "After every feed, doctor. Every single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 38.43,
      "end_seconds": 48.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "That's not right. It's not every feed. Maybe one or two a day, and it's only a little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 49.62,
      "end_seconds": 56.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "It is every feed, I do the night ones, you're asleep."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.0,
      "end_seconds": 68.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "I'll note that you remember it differently, and we'll see how he looks. Is he feeding well otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 69.55,
      "end_seconds": 81.32,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "He's hungry all the time. He takes about ninety millilitres, or maybe a hundred and twenty, I'm not sure. I don't measure carefully. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.04,
      "end_seconds": 89.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "That's helpful. Is he bottle-fed or breast-fed? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.63,
      "end_seconds": 94.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Formula only. We changed formula last month. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.13,
      "end_seconds": 99.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Why did you change it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 102.29,
      "end_seconds": 111.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "My sister says he's allergic to cow's milk formula, but I don't know what the reaction was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.11,
      "end_seconds": 124.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll note that. Is he vomiting forcefully, or is it just milk coming up? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 124.95,
      "end_seconds": 128.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Just milk dribbling out, mostly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.94,
      "end_seconds": 135.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Is there any green or bloody vomit, or a swollen tummy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 136.98,
      "end_seconds": 139.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No. None of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.93,
      "end_seconds": 147.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Has he had any fever, or diarrhoea? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 147.79,
      "end_seconds": 151.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.62,
      "end_seconds": 157.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "What have you been giving him, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 159.55,
      "end_seconds": 164.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Colic drops, five drops with each feed, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 166.48,
      "end_seconds": 173.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "She gives them, but I forget half the time when I do the evening feed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.26,
      "end_seconds": 183.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Thank you for being honest. I'll weigh him and check his temperature. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 186.48,
      "end_seconds": 191.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "He's been gaining, the health visitor said so. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.7,
      "end_seconds": 211.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Weight 6.2 kilograms, temperature 36.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 214.38,
      "end_seconds": 216.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Is that good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.35,
      "end_seconds": 227.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "That's a healthy weight for three months. Let me feel his tummy and look at him. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 244.66,
      "end_seconds": 246.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.77,
      "end_seconds": 254.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "His tummy is soft, no lumps, and he looks well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 256.18,
      "end_seconds": 258.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "So he's fine? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.15,
      "end_seconds": 272.61,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "He seems well, and growing well. This sounds like reflux, which is very common at this age, and he's not showing any warning signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 274.79,
      "end_seconds": 278.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "What can we do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.01,
      "end_seconds": 290.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "I'd like to start a sachet of infant Gaviscon, one sachet with each feed, mixed in the milk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 291.93,
      "end_seconds": 294.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "And the drops? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.26,
      "end_seconds": 308.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.93,
      "text": "We can stop those for now. Keep him upright for twenty minutes after each feed, and try smaller, more frequent feeds."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 309.12,
      "end_seconds": 313.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I'll do the evening ones properly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.69,
      "end_seconds": 323.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Come back in three weeks, or sooner if he vomits forcefully, goes green, or stops feeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 326.28,
      "end_seconds": 329.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "We will. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
